        },
        {
          "concern": "A force-find option can persistently change filters, and a semantic tag value differs from its serialized compatibility form.",
          "response": "The historical documentation explicitly preserves the warning that dropping view filters persists. Full lint discussion supplies no blanket read-only promise for get/find names.",
          "applied": "getViewIndexForMsgHdr can call setMailView(All, null) and clear showUnreadOnly, retrying native lookup. setMailView stores the caller tag value without a colon and adds the compatibility colon only at database persistence; empty data persists as an empty string. Current helper still has these side effects. Historical annotation srting is string in the frozen source; the inspected force-find caller passes null, so the actual permitted input must be checked rather than inferred from that scalar annotation.",
          "outcome": "The existing side-effect and representation proposals are reused without requiring an options-object rewrite or a legacy method rename. No direct force-find regression was added here and no persisted-settings scenario was run. No new user rule is created."
        }
